the 'par' blocks 'ptrWrite' and 'ptrRead' run apart: 'p' and 'q' may be the same memory
the 'par' blocks 'scale' and 'square' run as one block
the 'par' blocks 'c1' and 'c2' run as one block
the 'par' blocks 'c1+c2' and 'c3' run as one block
the 'par' blocks 'shiftA' and 'shiftB' run apart: 'y' is written by one and used at another index by the other
the 'par' blocks 'redA' and 'redB' run apart: the second uses what the first reduces
the 'par' blocks 'goalA' and 'goalB' run apart: their goals differ
the 'par' blocks 'callA' and 'callB' run apart: a body calls a function other than a maths one, or leaves its loop
the 'par' blocks 'rangeA' and 'rangeB' run apart: their ranges differ
the 'par' blocks 'nameA' and 'nameB' run apart: the second body already uses the first loop's variable name
the 'par' blocks 'glob1' and 'glob2' run as one block
